    answer: --why-not repeats in lockstep with rejected options (AUG-057)
    
    A single --why-not stays a shared scalar reason (legacy shape). Repeated
    --why-not values are stored per rejected option (option id + label + reason,
    structured prefix per-option-v1) and dump renders each pair; an arity mismatch
    is refused by name before any write. VERBS.md documents the arity.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
